---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Views from '../components/Views.astro';
import Glyph from '../components/Glyph.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { work } from '../data/work';
import { bookingUrl } from '../data/booking';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base>

<!-- 1. Statement. The three lines of the heading are also the key to the mark: square, circle, both. -->
<section class="hero container">
  <div class="hero-main">
    <p class="eyebrow">Automation and Intelligence Specialist</p>
    <h1 class="statement">
      <span class="line"><span>Dependable systems.</span> <Glyph kind="square"/></span>
      <span class="line"><em>Better judgement.</em> <Glyph kind="circle"/></span>
      <span class="line"><span>Designed together.</span> <Glyph kind="both"/></span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">I design the processes, tools and learning that help people do meaningful work, develop their own capability and adapt as things change.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="#work">Explore the work <Icon kind="down"/></a>
      <a class="text-link" href="#contact">Discuss an engagement <Icon kind="down"/></a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <aside class="hero-aside">
    <img src={`${base}/finlay-mccall.jpg`} alt="Dr Finlay McCall" width="450" height="450"/>
    <p class="proof"><span>PhD in Education · University of Canberra</span> <span>Learning design · Systems architecture · Research translation</span></p>
  </aside>
</section>

<!-- 2. The philosophy, as three views of one practice. -->
<Views/>

<!-- 3. Evidence. A ruled index: every case answers the same questions in the same places. -->
<section id="work" class="container section">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p>
    <div class="head-body">
      <h2>Different settings.<br/><em>One design practice.</em></h2>
      <p>From a professional’s first automation to a historical journal brought to life, the question is the same: what can systems support, and what do people need to understand, judge or create?</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ul class="work-index">
    {work.map(item => (
      <li class="work-row">
        <span class="work-num">{item.number}</span>
        <div class="work-main">
          <p class="work-cat"><span class="sr-only"> / </span>{item.category}</p>
          <h3><a href={`${base}/work/${item.slug}/`}>{item.title}</a></h3>
          <ul class="terms">{item.motif.map(term => <li>{term}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
        <p class="work-summary">{item.summary}</p>
        <div class="work-meta">
          <span class="status">{item.status}</span>
          <span class="read">Read the case study <Icon kind="next"/></span>
        </div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</section>

<!-- 4. The engagement. These ARE stages, so this is the one place the site uses a numbered sequence. -->
<section id="approach" class="sheet section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The engagement</p>
      <div class="head-body">
        <h2>A useful system.<br/><em>The capability to own it.</em></h2>
        <p>The deliverable is more than a recommendation or a tool. It is a coherent way forward, grounded in evidence, with people able to use and adapt what we build.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="method">
      <li><span>01</span><h3>Understand</h3><p>Discover the work, people, source material and constraints.</p></li>
      <li><span>02</span><h3>Frame</h3><p>Develop an evidence-backed brief, priorities and intended outcomes.</p></li>
      <li><span>03</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Create a practical workflow, learning experience or publishing system.</p></li>
      <li><span>04</span><h3>Transfer</h3><p>Develop capability through guided practice and usable documentation.</p></li>
      <li><span>05</span><h3>Review</h3><p>Check what works, what needs revision and what to evaluate next.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="approach-note">
      <h3>A shared record of the work</h3>
      <p>An evolving project website or workspace brings the brief, evidence, decisions and implementation together. Internal material stays private. The public case study tells only the part that can responsibly be shared.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 5. Offers. -->
<section class="container section" id="engage">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Work with me</p>
    <div class="head-body">
      <h2>Start with the work<br/><em>you want to make possible.</em></h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="offers">
    <article><h3>Clarify the opportunity</h3><p>An evidence-backed brief, a map of capability and workflow needs, and a practical implementation direction.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Design and build</h3><p>A bounded system, learning environment or publishing workflow, with clear review points and documentation.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Develop capability</h3><p>Coaching and supported practice that help people understand, maintain and adapt their own tools and processes.</p></article>
  </div>
  <p class="engage-invitation"><a class="text-link" href="#contact">Discuss what would help <Icon kind="down"/></a></p>
</section>

<!-- 6. Experience. The portrait now sits in the opening statement, so this section is text only. -->
<section id="experience" class="container section">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Experience & research</p>
    <div class="head-body prose">
      <h2>Education is the thread.<br/><em>Practice is the test.</em></h2>
      <p>My work connects teaching and assessment, teacher development, process improvement and research-led human–AI design. I bring that experience to organisational, educational and creative work.</p>
      <p>I hold a PhD in Education from the University of Canberra. My doctoral research examined curriculum and course design for human–AI collaboration. I currently work as Project Manager and Research Assistant on a UC and ACT Education Directorate project exploring teachers’ use of generative AI.</p>
      <p>I’m interested in employment and engagements that bring learning design, agent workflows, research translation and responsible AI practice together.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${base}/experience/`}>Explore experience & research <Icon kind="next"/></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 7. Contact. -->
<section id="contact" class="contact section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Employment · Engagements · Creative collaborations</p>
    <h2>What are you trying<br/><em>to make possible?</em></h2>
    <p>Bring a project, a process you’d like to improve, or a question about where AI could help. We’ll discuss what you need and whether working together would be useful.</p>
    <a class="button light" href={bookingUrl}>Book an introductory conversation <Icon kind="out"/></a>
    <p class="contact-alternative">Prefer email, or can’t find a suitable time? <a data-email href="#contact"><span data-email-text><noscript>hi [at] finlaymccall.com</noscript></span></a></p>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
